# Mastering B2 — real progress & “done”

## Real percent only (everywhere)

- **Never** write progress just because the learner **opened** a page or flipped speaking questions.
- **Never** invent engagement placeholders (old bug: auto **35%** / floor **60%**).
- Written tasks: record only after **Check** with a real score → `recordCheck` / `recordCheckFromDom(correct, total)`.
- Speaking / Discussion: record only when they press **Done** on the last step (typically **100%**). Do **not** call `record` from `render()` / on load / on Next.
- Hub badges show that exercise’s stored % — if nothing was submitted, show **no** percent (not started).

## Done threshold

- **Done / Passed** only if best score is **80–100%** (`PASS_THRESHOLD = 80` in `js/mastering-b2-skill-progress.js`).
- In progress: `0 < percent < 80` → show **%**, not ✓ / “done”.

## Hub vs exercise cards

| Card type | Attributes | Status source |
|-----------|------------|---------------|
| Skill folder on `unitN.html` | `data-mb2-hub="skill"` + `data-mb2-skill` | **Every required** leaf in `UNIT_SKILL_EXERCISES[unit][skill]` ≥ 80% (missing = not done) |
| Leaf exercise | `data-mb2-unit` + `data-mb2-skill` + **`data-mb2-ex`** — **no** `hub="skill"` | That **exact** `exerciseId` only |

When you **add a new exercise** under a skill, also add its `data-mb2-ex` to **`UNIT_SKILL_EXERCISES`** in `js/mastering-b2-skill-progress.js`. Otherwise the skill folder can keep the green ✓ from older completed items only.

**Forbidden:**

- `data-mb2-hub="skill"` on a single worksheet (false whole-skill “done”).
- Loose `exerciseId` matching (`get` ↔ `get-speak`) — use **exact** ids.
- Treating “all stored rows ≥ 80%” as skill done when the catalog lists more activities.

## Auto helper

`js/mastering-b2-exercise-auto.js`: harvest score after Check; if no score → **write nothing**. Done/Save → 100% only for explicit completion labels.

## Cleanup

`purgePhantomScores()` (once per browser via `masteringB2ProgressPurgeV3`) drops old 35% engagement rows and speaking/discussion browse scores under 100%.
